\[X_{2}=(-2\ln U_1)^{1/2}\sin 2\pi U_2 will be a pair of independent normal random deviates with mean zero and unit variance. This procedure can be modified by calculating cos 2\pi U and sin 2\pi U using an acceptance rejection method; e.g., (1) generate (U_1, U_2); (2) if (2U_1-1)^2+(2U_2-1)^2\leq 1 generate a third uniform deviate U_3, otherwise reject the pair and start over; (3) calculate

